{"agent":"fix-onboard","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The widened stop pattern is not needed for the checkbox bug and drops continuation metadata. The previous condition already breaks on `_CHECK.match`, so `+ [ ]` and `1. [ ]` siblings end the scan without this change. Given `- [ ] task` then an indented `  + keep this note` or `  1. detail` and then `  needs: other`, line 330 now matches the non-checkbox `+`/`1.` line and breaks before `_NEEDS`/`_GLOBS`/`_RESOURCES` are considered. Those same lines used to stay in the continuation (indent greater than the task, not a `-`/`*` marker), so `needs: other` was still seen. The import now silently fails to attach that metadata.","digest":"dec9d5102bbfab6a","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/importer/_titles.py:330","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/importer/_titles.py:330"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The rewritten stop still treats any indented `-`/`*` line as the end of the continuation, which drops metadata the new test says must be kept. `_CHECK` already ends the scan on a real box, and the indent check already ends it on a sibling at the same depth; `re.match(r\"\\s*[-*]\\s\", ln)` only adds a break for *deeper* dash/star notes. Given `- [ ] **T.1** first` then `  - keep this note` then `  **Needs:** T.0`, the note matches that pattern and the scan breaks before `_NEEDS`, so `needs` is empty. The added test only covers `+` and `1.`, so this common nested-bullet case still fails.","digest":"0a74a3e5fe58d142","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/importer/_titles.py:330","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/importer/_titles.py:330"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":1,"delta_from":"c7ea2bdcfd151b652af8d47bd5803455a9a1867d","delta_raised":["0a74a3e5fe58d142"],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":2426,"diff_sha":"dcdf753bf258ac51c03ea9d78f546505b3033b